.tl 'NARC(I)'12/17/75'NARC(I)

NAME
	narc - source archiver

SYNOPSIS
	narc file -k1 a11 ... a1n ... -km am1 ... amn

DESCRIPTION
	narc____ is a revision of the unix archiver (ar__ (i)) to exploit the
new file system. The action of narc is determined by a left-to-right
scan of the command. The valid keys are:

.in 30
.mk
.ti 14
-d f1 ... fn
.br
.rt
The named files are deleted from the library.

.mk
.ti 14
-r f1 ... fn
.br
.rt
The named files are replaced.

.mk
.ti 14
-m f1 ... fn
.br
.rt
The named files are replaced if their modification date is more
recent than the copy in the archive.

.mk
.ti 14
-i k f1 ... fn
.br
.rt
The named files are placed before the k_ file in the library.

.mk
.ti 14
-x f1 ... fn
.br
.rt
The named file are extracted from the library. If no files are specified, then
all files are extracted.

.mk
.ti 14
-a f1 ... fn
.br
.rt
The named files are appended to the archive. If the archive does not exist, it is
created.

.mk
.ti 14
-l
.br
.rt
The archive contents are listed.


.in 0
FILES
	narc.tmp - work file

BUGS
	Generally, file names must be in the correct order. This is rediculous, and
narc should be fixed to eliminate this.
